plication/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: corrected the false premise that External Integration already had macOS. It is currently Ubuntu-only; the ADR now explicitly assigns the later implementation ticket to add a dedicated ubuntu-latest + macos-latest Pandoc replay matrix. Split compound acceptance criteria and tagged the external Gerrit HOLD/merge outcomes operator-attested with their concrete evidence.","timestamp":1786716789451512001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DRAFT CRITIQUE (architecture-decisions gate, 2026-08-14). The proposed ADR 0096, ADR 0095 partial-supersession banner, ADR index/number marker, and transitional docs/architecture.md update are drafted locally; no implementation or test routing changed.\n\n1. Claims lacking research citations: none outstanding. All five OSS links were HTTP-validated at their pinned SHAs; the Rust citation was corrected from the standalone-guide repository to rust-lang/rust/src/doc/rustc-dev-guide at 059bf4a660dd. Timing and assertion-map claims cite run 31798375024 and umbrella ticket 4f50-b1f2-78af-4326.\n2. Internal inconsistencies: none outstanding after correction. docs/architecture.md now says ADR 0095 every-assertion-live routing remains current until the separate implementation lands, rather than falsely describing the proposed boundary as already active. ADR 0096 is Status: Proposed and carries Superseded by: N/A.\n3. Missing constraints: the draft now states the existing external workflow is Ubuntu-only and requires the implementation to add an Ubuntu+macOS Pandoc matrix. It explicitly accepts weekly detection delay and lower-cadence runner contention. It also requires any future fixture-changing Gerrit change to run External Integration Tests against the exact proposed ref via a temporary GitHub mirror branch before those bytes become the new compatibility baseline. No unresolved constraint remains.\n4. Conflicts with documented decisions: only ADR 0095 conflicts. The same change marks exactly its every-conversion-assertion-live clause partially superseded and states every production renderer, pin, safety, platform, degradation, immutability, and cutover decision remains authoritative. No other ADR conflict was found.\n\nLocal draft guards already pass: gen_adr_index.py --check, check_adr_numbers.py, check_docs_index.py, git diff --check. Per the mandatory lifecycle, HOLD is blocked until the operator explicitly confirms this draft critique.","timestamp":1786717203388234001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DRAFT published for review: Gerrit change 1775, commit ce5497055598436de667260b52115234464bbc99, Change-Id Ia11fcda5c44d5fdcc432aba836af63e71cce4d6c. Local documentation/ADR guards and make lint pass; verify-commit-ticket resolves this ticket. The draft remains in DRAFT pending explicit operator confirmation of the recorded four-part draft critique; HOLD has not yet been entered and implementation remains prohibited.","timestamp":1786717259060112001}],"created_at":1786716502273240001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f7fb3a8c-0120-4104-a922-117d4ba6c34f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"},{"link_uuid":"20571e8a-f844-4502-a201-704ce4cb76f1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d5b6-2eeb-edc8-4547"}],"description":"## Context\nGerrit Verify currently runs thousands of repeated real Pandoc subprocess conversions over the complete DC wiki corpus. Run 31798375024 attributed at least 184.32 seconds of the macOS critical path to two visible corpus phases alone. The operator confirmed the architecture research and approved moving the complete real-Pandoc corpus replay to the External Integration Tests workflow. Current ADR 0095 explicitly requires every conversion assertion to use the real binary, so this testing-boundary change requires a narrow superseding ADR before implementation.\n\n## Research decision\nPopular maintained OSS precedent supports committed golden/static outputs plus compact live boundary probes: Pandoc uses literal writer outputs; nbconvert and pypandoc use small real-Pandoc probes; Kubernetes client-go commits golden request/response fixtures; Rust compiletest uses blessed output snapshots. The approved design keeps three representative live corpus bodies (code_arrow, table, prose) plus existing compact provenance probes in Gerrit Verify. It preserves every assertion class against committed outputs in Verify. It moves complete real-Pandoc replay to a dedicated weekly/manual Pandoc job inside .github/workflows/external-integration.yml.\n\nThe current External Integration workflow has four Ubuntu-only jobs and no macOS runner. The later implementation ticket must therefore add an explicit pandoc-corpus-replay job whose matrix is os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest]; this is planned future implementation scope, not a claim about current workflow state and not part of this documentation-only ADR change. The job will run the complete replay on both platforms. Version drift and platform-specific binary fingerprints fail fast. Deterministic regeneration remains available. The 184.32-second figure is a lower-bound estimate; implementation must obtain paired A/B evidence.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a numbered ADR in docs/adr that narrowly supersedes ADR 0095 only where it mandates a real Pandoc process for every conversion assertion.\n- Preserve the production segmenting renderer, pin/provenance, Linux/macOS platform boundary, fallback behavior, and every safety/fixed-point/richness assertion class.\n- Amend ADR 0095 with a clear Superseded-by notice scoped to the testing-assurance clause.\n- Update docs/architecture.md with the authoritative hot-path versus external-integration verification boundary.\n- Record that the later implementation adds a dedicated pandoc-corpus-replay matrix to the currently Ubuntu-only external-integration workflow.\n- Regenerate the ADR index and number markers using scripts/gen_adr_index.py.\n- Run ADR numbering/index guards, documentation/link checks, lint, and the repository commit-ticket verifier.\n- Submit this documentation-only decision through Gerrit. Do not begin implementation until this ADR is merged after HOLD approval.\n\n## Expected file impact\n- docs/adr/0095-dc-segmenting-wiki-renderer.md\n- docs/adr/0096-pandoc-corpus-verification-boundary.md\n- docs/adr/README.md\n- docs/adr/.numbers/0096\n- docs/architecture.md\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The ADR cites the confirmed dependency research and named OSS precedents.\n- [ ] The ADR narrows supersession to the test execution boundary.\n- [ ] The ADR preserves every production renderer invariant.\n- [ ] Gerrit Verify retains three representative live corpus contracts plus the compact pin/provenance probes.\n- [ ] Every existing assertion class remains required against committed deterministic outputs in Gerrit Verify.\n- [ ] The ADR states that external-integration.yml is currently Ubuntu-only.\n- [ ] The ADR assigns future implementation of a dedicated pandoc-corpus-replay matrix with ubuntu-latest and macos-latest arms.\n- [ ] Complete real-Pandoc corpus replay is assigned to that weekly/manual external-integration job.\n- [ ] Installed Pandoc version drift fails fast.\n- [ ] Each supported platform binary fingerprint is verified.\n- [ ] Deterministic fixture regeneration remains documented.\n- [ ] The ADR states that 184.32 seconds is a one-run lower bound.\n- [ ] The ADR requires paired A/B implementation evidence.\n- [ ] ADR 0095 points to the superseding decision.\n- [ ] docs/architecture.md documents the verification boundary.\n- [ ] ADR number/index guards pass.\n- [ ] Documentation link guards pass.\n- [ ] No implementation code is included in this ADR change.\n- [ ] No test-routing change is included in this ADR change.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The ADR reaches HOLD in Gerrit; evidence is the Gerrit change id and HOLD announcement recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The ADR merges only after explicit approval; evidence is the approval identity and merge timestamp recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0095-dc-segmenting-wiki-renderer.md","reason":"Mark the testing-assurance clause as narrowly superseded."},{"path":"docs/adr/0096-pandoc-corpus-verification-boundary.md","reason":"Record the approved verification-boundary decision."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Regenerated ADR index."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0096","reason":"ADR number ownership marker."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Document the current Verify versus external-integration boundary."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d5b6-2eeb-edc8-4547"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c5405093-fb80-4a80-a39b-a97c91783032","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","pandoc","adr","performance"],"ticket_id":"a38f-e290-9585-40be","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: move complete Pandoc corpus replay to external integration","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["79d4a76b-2526-46cd-84b1-faba279d7e3d","4a3a4c62-5bfc-450a-b54a-70f5e2e5aa12","f7fb3a8c-0120-4104-a922-117d4ba6c34f","c92f1d76-608f-